{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And all the congregation of the children of Israel went out… and they came.</b> This verse indicates the zeal of Israel, for they brought the donation with zeal and diligence, and the women preceded them — and this is the language of the verse." "<b>And the men came upon the women.</b> For the expression על הנשים ('upon the women') indicates that the women came there first, and when the men came they already found the women there, who had brought their donation first. And this is a great virtue in the women, for in the matter of the calf they refused to give their ornaments, as it is written (Exodus 32): ״ויאמר להם אהרן פרקו נזמי הזהב אשר באזני נשיכם בניכם ובנותיכם״, and it is written (ibid.): ״ויתפרקו כל העם את נזמי הזהב אשר באזניהם״ — and it does not say 'in the ears of their wives,' because the women did not want this. And this is what Solomon hinted at concerning this (Ecclesiastes 7): ״אדם אחד מאלף מצאתי ואשה בכל אלה לא מצאתי״ — he alludes to what is written (Exodus 32): ״אלה אלהיך״." "<b>But</b> now, in the matter of the commandment of the donation for the Mishkan, they wanted to give their gold ornaments with great willingness, despite the fact that it is natural for women to delight and rejoice in their ornaments, and they are the very essence of their joy and desire. And they brought חח ונזם וטבעת עגיל וכומז — every gold utensil — and they preceded the men in this commandment, for thus the expression על indicates, in the manner of (Isaiah 7:2): ״נחה ארם על אפרים״ — for that war was against Ephraim, and Ephraim were there first." "<b>And in Pirkei</b> Rabbi Eliezer: the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the women their reward in this world and in the world to come, because this occurred on Rosh Chodesh — in this world, that they observe the watch of the New Moons more than the men, and in the world to come, that they are destined to be renewed like the New Moons, as it is said (Psalms 103:5): ״המשביע בטוב עדיך תתחדש כנשר נעוריכי״. And as for what the verse says, ״כל נדיב לב הביאו חח ונזם״ — and it is the women who bring them — it appears to me that the sense of the verse is as though it is suspended (מסורס), and its reading is: 'And the men came, every willing-hearted one, upon the women who brought חח ונזם.' And it says: ״וכל איש אשר נמצא אתו תכלת וארגמן״ — for the תכלת and the ארגמן were not available to everyone, but only to certain important people among them. And it further mentions: ״וכל אשר נמצא אתו עצי שטים״ — for they were still fewer who had שטים wood in their possession."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {2 "The citation (ישעיהו ז׳:ב׳) is given as written; the page reference is anomalous since the verse is Isaiah 7:2 — rendered as normalized.", 3 "The prooftext ״המשביע בטוב עדיך תתחדש כנשר נעוריכי״ (Psalms 103:5) is cited with suffixed pronouns (-יך) more familiar from Psalms 103:5's parallel phrasing; the verse citation is given as (תהילים ק״ג:ה׳), here normalized to Psalms 103:5."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:07:28.854494598Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}